# N20: Remix ParseGameRow splits one server row into several TriggerParse lines (scripts + #triggers):
# (a) a roomDesc preset is printed on its own and the rest of the row later (Game.cs:689-693 R);
#     real row shape from a tester's live capture (DESC shortened);
# (b) a stream-target change mid-row flushes the buffered text first (Game.cs:628-658, 2941-2956 R).
# The Lich glue delivers each row as ONE joined line.
INPUT #trigger {^\s*You also see the stairway} {#echo trig-own-line}
INPUT #trigger {^A stone-paved walkway lies to the west\.$} {#echo trig-desc-own-line}
INPUT #trigger {lies to the west\.\s+You also see} {#echo trig-joined}
INPUT #trigger {^PRE MID POST$} {#echo trig-whole}
INPUT #trigger {^PRE\s*$} {#echo trig-pre}
INPUT #trigger {^MID$} {#echo trig-mid}
INPUT #trigger {^ POST$} {#echo trig-post}
WAIT 100
IN <style id=""/><preset id='roomDesc'>A stone-paved walkway lies to the west.</preset>  You also see the stairway to the street.
WAIT 300
IN PRE <pushStream id='thoughts'/>MID<popStream/> POST
WAIT 300
IN DONETOK
WAIT 300
